\ Deadline: the vocabulary and the sentence patterns. A pattern is the verb,
\ its prepositions and a frame per noun phrase: :find names the flag of the
\ thing understood when the phrase is left out, :search where the thing may
\ be (held, carried, on-ground, in-room), and whether it is taken first
\ (take), must be held (have) or may be several (many). The symbol after a
\ pattern names the action it performs.

\ ---- words the parser passes over ----

[ "a" "an" "the" "is" "are" "and" "of" "then" "all" "one" "but" "except" "."
  "," """" "y" "number" "minute" "back" "page" "carefully" "quietly"
  "slowly" "quickly" "briefly" "do" "you" "have" "was" "were" "your"
] buzz-words

\ ---- directions ----

"north" :north direction-word
"south" :south direction-word
"east" :east direction-word
"west" :west direction-word
"ne" :northeast direction-word
"nw" :northwest direction-word
"se" :southeast direction-word
"sw" :southwest direction-word
"up" :up direction-word
"down" :down direction-word
"in" :in direction-word
"out" :out direction-word

\ ---- words that mean the same as the first word, in every part of speech ----

